{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "actor": "cedar-4",
      "decision": "reuse",
      "ability": "probe",
      "reason": "Probe already supports nearby observation and paid physical investigation of owned samples without ingestion. The reported reference failures require an in-place item-resolution correction, not a separate investigation ability. Your recorded hazelnut is an appropriate target, subject to live ownership and quantity validation. Physical findings cannot establish nutrition, toxicity or food safety merely from appearance or handling.",
      "specification": "Hand off a versioned correction to probe, preserving its interface ID, existing mastery, costs and evidence history. Public parameters: target (exact object/item ID or resource:ID), mode (observe|trial), method, and confirmDestructive (default false). Resolve exact owned inventory IDs against authoritative inventory before spatial-object lookup; inventory items need no separate world-object registration. resource:ID must select an actual eligible stack and report its resolved ID; ambiguous selections require clarification. Never substitute another item for an unavailable exact ID. External subjects require visibility and actual interaction reach of 0.65 using shared geometry; inventory subjects are accessible to their owner. Before destructive execution, disclose the method, one-round duration, 0.5 energy cost, 0.1-unit sample consumption, required implements and modeled hazards; require explicit confirmation. Observation takes one round and 0.2 energy without consuming material. Support direct visual inspection and feasible manual physical trials using existing probe mechanics; validate method-specific requirements, and explain unavailable measurements rather than inventing results. No tool, assay, heat source or safety knowledge is supplied. For trials, reserve 0.1 unit from the selected stack, preserving origin, age and composition; record its actual disposition as consumed test material, never a second edible output. Store operation ID, owner, selected item, method, reserved fraction, paid effort and remaining work. Revalidate at execution; finish exactly once after the paid round. Cancellation, including death, returns unconsumed escrow exactly once to the surviving inventory or a ground stack at the actor's actual position; already consumed material and spent effort remain accounted for. No background work continues after cancellation. Observations and results retain actor, target, method, conditions, evidence event and uncertainty. Preserve existing verified findings and record the resolver correction separately from functional capability registration. Declare and validate subscriptions for trial-result, trial-material-consumed and information-confirmed; use failed for resolution or prerequisite failures. Implementation advances no simulation time and grants no items or learning rewards.",
      "experienceReview": "Reuse grounded-understanding rather than register a duplicate source. A completed observation or physical trial may emit information-confirmed with qualified=true only when it establishes genuinely new, method-supported information for the investigating actor. Mere target resolution, application, studying, failed trials and repeated known facts do not qualify. Use the existing temporary rule: amount 0.8, cap 1, duration 8 rounds, refresh repetition with a 12-round cooldown. Use its existing maintained rule: gain 0.035 per qualifying event and decay 0.0015 per round, under the registered bounded source saturation and global mental cap. No separate pleasure source is needed for sample handling itself. Unknown food safety remains unknown; neither feedback nor investigation changes nutrition, health or survival accounts.",
      "visualReview": "Show the resolved inventory sample and quantity, observation versus destructive-trial mode, disclosed costs, confirmation requirement and actual result. Bind result presentation to trial-result, material loss to trial-material-consumed, and qualified discovery feedback to information-confirmed. Replay must identify the real target, paid effort, consumed fraction and evidence limits. Do not depict ingestion, invented laboratory equipment, successful shell opening without an actual result, or a food-safety approval badge. Inventory inspection creates no world obstacle or duplicate sample.",
      "learning": 0
    }
  ]
}

